<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oberwart</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Felsőőr</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oberwart, in Hungarian Felsőőr, is a town in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgenland">Burgenland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, with a long-established Hungarian-speaking community descended from medieval border guards. On 4 October 1921, while western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> was being handed over to Austria, the Hungarian irregular commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pal-pronay">Pál Prónay</a> proclaimed the short-lived Banate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leitha">Leitha</a> there. It is now the administrative centre of Oberwart district.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oberwart.jpg" alt="Oberwart" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: C.Stadler/Bwag · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oberwart_-_Rathaus.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
